   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The future of probability or conjecture",
     "texto": [
      "In Italian the future is used very frequently to make logical deductions about a current situation that is not absolutely certain: **Sarà a casa** (he's probably at home / he must be at home now); **Che ore sono? — Saranno le tre** (what time is it? — It's probably three o'clock)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Conjecture about age or quantity",
     "texto": [
      "It is very common for estimating amounts, prices or approximate ages: **Quanti anni ha quella ragazza? — Avrà vent'anni** (how old is that girl? — She's probably about twenty); **Costerà circa cinquanta euro** (it will probably cost around fifty euros)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Temporal future versus conjecture",
     "columnas": [
